**AI usage rule:** AI can explain concepts, help debug *after* you've been stuck for 20 minutes, and review work you've finished. It never writes the week's core component. If AI writes it, the week doesn't count.

**Done means done:** a week is finished only when its "Done when" criteria are met and pushed. Don't start the next week early.

**Low-energy weeks:** if health or work flattens you, do the minimum: the blind rebuild plus 30 minutes of reading. The week stretches, and the plan doesn't restart.

**Buffer weeks:** week 7 is a buffer for catching up, resting or a mock interview, never new material. If you're more than a week behind by week 13, take a second buffer before week 14.

**Languages:** English, German, Hindi, Arabic. That's two Latin-script languages, one Devanagari and one right-to-left script, which exposes the real multilingual problems. All four are in both datasets.

**Datasets:**

- **Online Retail II (UCI):** about 1M transactions from a UK online wholesaler of giftware, many of whose customers are businesses. The basis of the churn project (weeks 1–3 and 7), the customer value models (week 4), the segmentation (week 5) and the real-data tests (week 6).
- **WikiANN (PAN-X)** on Hugging Face: NER with PER/ORG/LOC tags across many languages. Used in weeks 10–11 and 14.
- **XQuAD**: the same paragraphs and questions professionally translated into 11 languages. Your retrieval corpus and QA gold set for weeks 12–13.

